NAME
       drv - device drivers: what loaded, what did not

SYNOPSIS
       drv
       drv start <name>
       drv stop <name>
       drv autostart <name> on|off

DESCRIPTION
       Lists every driver built into the kernel with what became of it.

STATES
       running   it claimed at least one device here
       idle      built in, but nothing on this machine matches it; this
                 is the normal state for most drivers
       failed    it matched a device and could not bring it up - the
                 one worth looking into
       stopped   shut down, or not probed at boot

       The device column shows the vendor and device id it claimed, and
       uptime counts from when it started.

COMMANDS
       start       probe the hardware again. Useful after a driver has
                   been stopped, or to retry one that failed.
       stop        shut it down. Only drivers that know how can do
                   this; the rest say so and stay until the next boot.
       autostart   whether the driver is tried when a matching device
                   is found. Off means the device is left alone.

NOTES
       When a driver says failed, dmesg or dbgmon carries the reason:
       drivers log what they could not do.

SEE ALSO
       lspci(1), lsusb(1), dmesg(1), dbgmon(1), sysreport(1)
